docs {
  TRON gRPC API — unary methods of the `protocol.Wallet` (latest state) and
  `protocol.WalletSolidity` (confirmed state) services, served through Alchemy.

  **Endpoints:**
  - Mainnet: `https://tron-mainnet.g.alchemy.com/`
  - Nile testnet: `https://tron-testnet.g.alchemy.com/`

  **Auth:** send your Alchemy API key as gRPC metadata:
  `X-Token: <api_key>` (set `api_key` in your Bruno environment).

  **Protos:** the gateway does not expose server reflection, so the real
  TRON protos are bundled under `grpc/proto/` (source:
  https://github.com/tronprotocol/protocol). The entrypoint is
  `grpc/proto/api/api.proto`.

  **Bytes fields:** protobuf JSON encodes `bytes` as base64 of the raw bytes.
  For a TRON address, base58-decode it (or take the 21-byte hex form starting
  with `41`) and base64-encode: `echo 41E552...32CD0 | xxd -r -p | base64`.
}
